- op: discuss  # 908a
  at: '2026-05-09T04:49:50Z'  # 908a
  by: agent  # 908a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 908a
  clock: 4  # 908a
  nonce: 908a  # 908a
  message: "Fixed in PR #3589 (merged). Root cause was NOT a struct-extractor parser misclassification (verified: tree-sitter-rust 0.24.0 does not produce struct_item for #[derive(...)] or trait-bound positions, and candle-core/cuda_backend/mod.rs:85 literally is 'struct Clone;' — a real, intentional unit struct). Real root cause: rust.py's impl_item handler at lines 1090-1117 resolved trait_name without checking kind, so the LHS of 'impl Clone for VarBuilderArgs' (in candle-nn/var_builder.rs:23) bound to the candle-local 'struct Clone' instead of being treated as unresolved. Fix: require trait_sym.kind=='trait'; non-trait matches now fall through to the unresolved-trait branch (which suppresses Clone via _RUST_STD_TRAIT_NAMES). Test: test_impl_for_struct_does_not_resolve_to_struct_named_like_trait in TestRustTraitImplEdges. Same structural class as WI-zozuz BUG-03 (the inheritance-linker analogue, already fixed via Rust kind discipline at linkers/inheritance.py:197-206)."  # 908a
